# X-Security curated ClamAV .ndb signature set — definitions v1
#
# Format: Name:TargetType:Offset:HexSignature[:MinSize,MaxSize]
#
# TargetType 0 (any) is used deliberately: the engine applies no target-type
# filter, so a non-zero value would only raise the "target type ignored"
# counter. Offset '*' means the signature may match anywhere in the scanned
# byte stream — that includes the raw APK bytes AND decompressed ZIP entries
# (classes.dex, AndroidManifest.xml, ...) since the content scanner.
#
# --- Metasploit / msfvenom (android/meterpreter) ---
# "META-INF/SIGNFILE." — Rex::Zip's hardcoded JAR signature entry names are
# plainly visible in the ZIP directory structure of every default msfvenom APK.
Android.Tool.Metasploit.Signfile:0:*:4D4554412D494E462F5349474E46494C452E
# dex type descriptors of the staged payload (inside decompressed classes.dex)
Android.Trojan.Metasploit.Stage:0:*:636F6D2F6D65746173706C6F69742F73746167652F
Android.Trojan.Metasploit.AndroidPayload:0:*:636F6D2F6D65746173706C6F69742F616E64726F69647061796C6F61642F
# stageless payload root class (inside decompressed classes.dex)
Android.Trojan.Metasploit.Stageless:0:*:636F6D2E6D65746173706C6F69742E6D657465727072657465722E416E64726F69644D65746572707265746572
# binary AndroidManifest.xml stores strings as UTF-16LE (inside the
# decompressed manifest entry)
Android.Trojan.Metasploit.Manifest:0:*:63006F006D002E006D00650074006100730070006C006F00690074002E0073007400610067006500
#
# --- Packers / protectors (risk indicators) ---
